{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Br3jGZ4jnaJmLbhvmng8vw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a **single-user personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, plain-text source of truth). Here's what it grounds out to:\n\n- **What it is at the core:** a GTD-style task/project manager whose source of truth is plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, per-domain files under `domains/`, plus `CANCELLED.md`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md` archives). No database, no binary formats â€” everything stays readable by any CLI or editor.\n\n- **What it ships (the deliverable):** `anchor_gui.py` â€” a self-contained, Python-stdlib-only HTTP server that renders an interactive dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reads/writes the markdown directly, and logs every change. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` (auto-start), so the user just opens the browser. A CLI twin (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Task lifecycle + reliability:** tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, all via API endpoints and CLI commands. A daily self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, exercising file integrity, every endpoint, and the full R&D surface against stubs, then writes a dated health report.\n\n- **The major built-out feature â€” the R&D \"cockpit\":** a per-project \"mission control\" for running the **trio of skills** (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) as durable, server-side sessions. It has been built and merged through **four versions** (v2 sessions/summaries/grass, v3 \"Mission Control,\" v4 \"Project Cockpit\"). Concretely it provides: real ConPTY terminals (xterm.js, the one declared `pywinpty` exception to stdlib-only), per-session git-worktree isolation, cached/validated AI summaries, lane status-light tiles with inline expanding panels, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini, Gemini research-only), cost/tokens/time rollups, a grass-idea board, and type-aware deliverable launching.\n\n- **Branding/positioning:** the surface is dressed as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\" â€” but functionally it remains John's private one-machine system, not a distributed product.\n\nThe North Star claims you cited are specifically about that R&D cockpit sub-surface â€” its goal of a \"calm, single-screen cockpit\" per project where each lane shows one honest status light and opening a session \"feels exactly like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session.\" That's the most actively-developed layer on top of the underlying markdown task manager."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b2a29f9-8b3d-4cf1-8149-5bacceff3e27","uuid":"9ff14972-498a-4808-9158-888e5b0828c8","request_id":"req_011Cc1hwq4cCFnQYEE5xV2Vv"}
